## A1 (blocker) — a collapsed zone is inert on release too

The release decision in `onZoneItemPointerEnd` now checks the hidden state before it can settle an
item back into the zone:

```js
var detached;
if (cancelled) detached = item.element.classList.contains("is-detached");
else if (zoneHidden) detached = true;               // inert collapsed zone
else detached = pointerOutsideZone(...) > ZONE_RELEASE_DISTANCE;
```

Probe: both items out → zone hidden → grab the notepad, move the pointer to the hidden zone's old
centre, release.

```
before release:  zone classes [demo-zone__card, is-collapsed], data-zone-visible=false,
                 visibility hidden, opacity 0; both items detached;
                 status "Zone hidden — drag the two items together to form a new zone."
after release:   zone classes [demo-zone__card, is-collapsed], data-zone-visible=false,
                 visibility hidden, opacity 0; both items still detached;
                 status unchanged
```

The item stays free and the zone cannot re-dock or reveal itself. Docking during the 180 ms exit
(before the zone is hidden) still cancels the exit, and grouping is still the way back.

## A3 (major) — grouped zone re-orients and re-fits on resize

One grouped zone (created at 1440×900: horizontal, 526 × 174 px at world (124.4, 126.7)) is resized
with the same page (no reload); `layout()`/`ResizeObserver` call `syncZoneGeometry`, which recomputes
the orientation from the current item sizes and the world, toggles `is-horizontal`, clamps the zone
(into the surface and below the toolbar) and repositions the docked items onto their new slots.

```
1440 x 900 (grouped):  orientation horizontal, zone 526 x 174 at (124.4, 126.7),
                       insideWorld true, toolbarOverlap 0
390 x 844:             orientation vertical, zone 274 x 275 at (0, 126.7),
                       world 356 x 744, insideWorld true, toolbarOverlap 0,
                       notepad (17, 143.7) 240 x 88.6, window (17, 244.7) 240 x 140,
                       clipped: false / false
900 x 844:             orientation horizontal, zone 526 x 174 at (0, 126.7),
                       insideWorld true, clipped false / false
901 x 844:             orientation horizontal, zone 526 x 174 at (0, 126.7), insideWorld true
1440 x 900 again:      orientation horizontal, zone 526 x 174 at (0, 126.7),
                       insideWorld true, toolbarOverlap 0, clipped false / false
```

The photo is no longer clipped (the round-1 bug: horizontal 17–543 px against a 16–374 px surface,
152 px clipped, while page overflow was still 0). The zone remains fully inside the world rectangle
in all four states, both items are visible and the A/B edge stays at exactly one element.

## Collapse (unchanged from round 1, re-measured)

```
docked:            zone 274 x 275, opacity 1, visible, layout=docked
one item out:      zone still visible, opacity 1 (zone stays while an item is inside)
both items out:    opacity 1 -> 0, scale 1 -> 0.96 over --motion-panel (180 ms)
timeline (ms, opacity, scale):
   5, 1.00, 1.000      22, 0.60, 0.9839     39, 0.32, 0.9729
  55, 0.16, 0.9665     72, 0.07, 0.9630     89, 0.03, 0.9612
 106, 0.01, 0.9604    (end) 0.00, 0.9600
after the exit:    [is-collapsed], opacity 0, visibility hidden, data-zone-visible=false
mid-fade capture:  transition paused via the Web Animations API at 18 ms: opacity 0.57,
                   transform scale 0.9829 (hide timer stretched only for the capture; the
                   timeline above is the real, unpaused curve)
