Docking during the exit still cancels it (measured in round 1: at 70 ms the zone is at opacity 0.16
with `[is-leaving]`; after docking the notepad the zone is back at opacity 1 and visible).

## Grouping (re-measured)

```
overlap below threshold:  rect overlap 0.185 (18.5 % of the smaller area), centres 101 px apart
                          -> no grouping, zone stays hidden
overlap above threshold:  12 px further the geometric overlap is 0.308 (30.8 %) -> grouping
grouped zone:             layout=grouped, orientation=horizontal, zone 526 x 174 at (124.4, 126.7),
                          insideWorld true, toolbarOverlap 0
slots:                    notepad 240 x 88.6 at (141.4, 143.7), window 240 x 140 at (393.4, 143.7)
                          (16 px zone padding, original 12 px gap, side by side)
status:                   "Items grouped into a new zone."
centre rule (50 % zoom):  overlap 0.106 (10.6 % < 25 %) with centres 58 px -> no grouping; after
                          moving closer the items group with the same 10.6 % overlap because the
                          centres are within 48 screen px
grouped near the top:     zone top clamped to y=74 px = toolbar bottom (66 px world) + --space-8,
                          toolbarOverlap 0, both items docked and visible
```

